Description: wrapper for WhatsApp Web in a window of its own (alpha)
 Querencia Web Wrapper (German: Querencia Webhülle) shows WhatsApp Web in a
 window of its own, with the classic menu bar of Querencia Desktop. It
 keeps the sign-in, announces new messages through the notifications of the
 desktop, shows the number of unread messages in the window title, saves
 downloads to the Downloads folder and checks spelling. Calls are not
 possible: the web engine of Ubuntu is built without WebRTC.
 .
 This program is not a product of WhatsApp or Meta and is not affiliated
 with them; WhatsApp is a trademark of its owner and is named only to say
 which web page the program shows.
 .
 The package is optional: it is offered by Querencia but is not part of
 the default installation (querencia-desktop). Until version 0.1.1 the
 program was called Querencia Messages (querencia-nachrichten); on its
 first start it takes over the sign-in and the settings by renaming the
 folders of that name.
 .
 The web pages run in WebKitGTK's own sandbox (bubblewrap, a dependency of
 libwebkitgtk-6.0-4). The interface is English with a German translation
 (gettext); the translations of the shared libraries come with
 querencia-shell.
 .
 Querencia Desktop is developed with AI tools; every change is reviewed
 and accepted by the project owner.
 This is an alpha release.
